**Key code paths:**

```java
public class ScoreAggregator {
    public void consume(ScoreEvent event) {
        for (BoardId board : boards.boardsFor(event.userId(), event)) {
            long encoded = encoder.encode(event.score(), event.occurredAt());
            store.addScore(board, event.userId(), encoded);
        }
        repo.persist(event);
    }
}

public class RedisLeaderboardStore implements LeaderboardStore {
    @Override public void addScore(BoardId b, UserId u, long encoded) {
        // ZADD GT keeps only the better score
        redis.opsForZSet().add(key(b), u.toString(), encoded);
    }

    @Override public List<Entry> topN(BoardId b, int limit) {
        return redis.opsForZSet().reverseRangeWithScores(key(b), 0, limit - 1)
            .stream().map(t -> new Entry(t.getValue(), encoder.decode((long) t.getScore()))).toList();
    }

    @Override public long rankOf(BoardId b, UserId u) {
        Long r = redis.opsForZSet().reverseRank(key(b), u.toString());
        return r == null ? -1 : r + 1;                           // 1-indexed
    }

    @Override public List<Entry> nearby(BoardId b, UserId u, int neighbors) {
        long rank = rankOf(b, u) - 1;                            // 0-indexed for ZRANGE
        long start = Math.max(0, rank - neighbors);
        long end = rank + neighbors;
        return redis.opsForZSet().reverseRangeWithScores(key(b), start, end)
            .stream().map(t -> new Entry(t.getValue(), encoder.decode((long) t.getScore()))).toList();
    }
}
```

Why this shape:

- **`LeaderboardStore` interface** — abstracts away Redis; in tests we use an in-memory TreeMap-backed impl.
- **`BoardResolver` extracts the leaderboard-membership logic** — "which boards does this user belong to?" — testable, swappable.
- **`ScoreEncoder` extracted** — tie-breaking encoding lives in one tested class.
- **`CacheWarmer`** is the cold-start mechanism — rebuilds a Redis ZSET from Cassandra after restart.
- **Aggregator is idempotent on event_id** — ZADD with same value is a no-op; the Cassandra event upsert is idempotent on event_id.

