**Key code paths:**

```java
public class UploadService {
    public UploadPlan planUpload(String path, List<String> chunkHashes) {
        Set<String> existing = registry.findExisting(chunkHashes);
        List<MissingChunk> missing = chunkHashes.stream()
            .filter(h -> !existing.contains(h))
            .map(h -> new MissingChunk(h, presigner.putUrl(s3KeyFor(h))))
            .toList();
        UploadSession session = sessionStore.create(path, chunkHashes);
        return new UploadPlan(session.id(), missing, existing);
    }

    public FileVersion commit(String sessionId) {
        UploadSession session = sessionStore.get(sessionId);
        verifyAllChunksUploaded(session);                               // HEAD requests to S3
        registry.incrementRef(session.chunkHashes());
        File file = metadataService.createOrUpdateFile(session.path(), session.chunkHashes());
        sync.publish(file.ownerId(), new FileChanged(file.id(), file.currentVersion()));
        return file.currentVersion();
    }
}

public class SyncService {
    public ChangeBatch pollChanges(long userId, String cursor, Duration timeout) {
        long sinceSeq = decode(cursor);
        List<SyncEvent> immediate = repo.fetchSince(userId, sinceSeq, 100);
        if (!immediate.isEmpty()) return toBatch(immediate);
        return waiterRegistry.waitForUser(userId, sinceSeq, timeout);    // long-poll
    }

    public void publish(long userId, FileChanged event) {
        repo.appendEvent(userId, event);
        waiterRegistry.signal(userId);                                   // wake any pollers
        notify.pushToDevices(userId, event);
    }
}
```

Why this shape:

- **`ChunkRegistry` interface** — today PostgreSQL, could swap to a sharded KV (DynamoDB) for hash lookups at higher scale.
- **`PresignedUrlFactory` interface** — lets us swap S3 for GCS/Azure Blob without touching upload logic.
- **`UploadSession` is server-side state** — tracks which chunks the client claimed plus which have arrived. Verified at commit.
- **Sync uses a waiter registry for long-poll** — in-process map of `userId → waiting threads` woken on publish; reduces tail latency vs polling Kafka per-poll.
- **GC is its own job** — chunk reference counts are eventual; race with in-flight uploads handled by 7-day grace.

