**Key code paths:**

```java
public class TranscodingScheduler {
    public void schedule(VideoId id, S3Key source) {
        List<TimeRange> chunks = splitter.splitByKeyframes(source);
        for (RenditionSpec spec : LADDER) {
            for (int i = 0; i < chunks.size(); i++) {
                kafka.publish("transcode.tasks",
                    new ChunkTask(id, source, chunks.get(i), i, spec));
            }
        }
    }
}

public class TranscodingWorker {
    public ChunkResult execute(ChunkTask task) {
        Path local = storage.fetchRange(task.source(), task.timeRange());
        Path output = ffmpeg.transcode(local, task.renditionSpec());
        double vmaf = quality.vmafScore(local, output);
        if (vmaf < THRESHOLD) {
            return ChunkResult.failed("vmaf_below_threshold");
        }
        S3Key uploaded = storage.put(task.outputKey(), output);
        coordinator.onChunkComplete(task.videoId(), task.id(), uploaded);
        return ChunkResult.ok(uploaded);
    }
}

public class TranscodingCoordinator {
    public void onChunkComplete(VideoId id, TaskId taskId, S3Key uploaded) {
        chunkProgress.markComplete(id, taskId);
        if (chunkProgress.allCompleteFor(id)) {
            finalizeVideo(id);
        }
    }

    public void finalizeVideo(VideoId id) {
        for (RenditionSpec rendition : LADDER) {
            Manifest m = packager.packageRendition(chunkProgress.chunksFor(id, rendition), rendition);
            storage.put("manifests/" + id + "/" + rendition + "/index.m3u8", m.bytes());
        }
        Manifest master = packager.packageMaster(LADDER);
        storage.put("manifests/" + id + "/master.m3u8", master.bytes());
        metadata.markAvailable(id, LADDER);
    }
}
```

Why this shape:

- **`StorageClient` interface** — S3 today; could be GCS or a self-hosted object store.
- **`FfmpegRunner` is its own collaborator** — lets us A/B-test encoder versions, settings, hardware (GPU vs CPU).
- **`QualityValidator` extracted** — VMAF or PSNR or SSIM; swap freely.
- **Coordinator tracks chunk completion per video** — finalization happens once when all chunks land; race-free via per-video locks.
- **Per-title bitrate selection** can be added by computing a content-complexity score in `TranscodingScheduler` before publishing tasks.

