**Key code paths:**

```java
public class MatchingService {
    private final BlockingQueue<TripRequest> incoming = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();

    public void submit(TripRequest req) { incoming.add(req); }

    @Scheduled(fixedRate = 2000)
    public void runBatch() {
        List<TripRequest> batch = new ArrayList<>();
        incoming.drainTo(batch);
        if (batch.isEmpty()) return;

        Map<TripRequest, List<Driver>> candidates = batch.stream()
            .collect(toMap(r -> r, r -> geo.nearbyDrivers(
                r.pickupLat(), r.pickupLng(), 5000, r.vehicleType())));

        List<Match> matches = optimizer.optimize(batch, candidates);

        for (Match m : matches) {
            offerDispatcher.sendOffer(m.driverId(), m.trip())
                .thenAccept(resp -> {
                    if (resp.accepted()) {
                        tripService.transition(m.trip().id(), Event.ACCEPTED);
                    } else {
                        tripService.transition(m.trip().id(), Event.OFFER_DECLINED);
                        offerNextCandidate(m.trip(), candidates.get(m.trip()));
                    }
                });
        }
    }
}

public class TripService {
    public Result transition(TripId id, Event event) {
        Trip trip = repo.loadById(id);
        State next = sm.nextState(trip.status(), event);
        if (next == null) return Result.illegalTransition();
        int updated = repo.updateStatus(id, trip.version(), next);
        if (updated == 0) return Result.retry();
        repo.appendEvent(id, TripEvent.of(event, next));
        wsHub.pushTo(trip.riderId(), TripUpdateFrame.of(trip, next));
        wsHub.pushTo(trip.driverId(), TripUpdateFrame.of(trip, next));
        return Result.ok(next);
    }
}

public class RedisH3Index implements GeospatialIndex {
    @Override public List<Driver> nearbyDrivers(double lat, double lng, double radiusM, String vt) {
        long centerCell = h3.geoToH3(lat, lng, 8);
        List<Long> cells = h3.kRing(centerCell, 2);          // ~19 cells
        return cells.stream()
            .flatMap(c -> redis.opsForSet().members("drivers:cell:" + c).stream())
            .map(this::loadDriver)
            .filter(d -> d.vehicleType().equals(vt) && d.status() == AVAILABLE)
            .filter(d -> haversine(lat, lng, d.lat(), d.lng()) < radiusM)
            .toList();
    }
}
```

Why this shape:

- **`GeospatialIndex` interface** — H3 in Redis today; could swap to a managed geospatial DB (e.g., PostGIS) for a smaller deployment.
- **`MatchOptimizer` extracted** — the bipartite algorithm is testable, swappable, and tunable independently.
- **`OfferDispatcher` returns a Future** — timeouts handled cleanly; declined offers route to the next candidate without blocking the batch loop.
- **`TripStateMachine` is its own class** — the legal-transition table powers both the service and the API ("can this trip be cancelled?").
- **WebSocketHub abstracts the regional hub topology** — push to user_id, hub figures out which Connection Service holds the socket.
